p>\n                \n                <p class=\"meta\" style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem;\">\n                    Analyzed with qwen3:30b-instruct\n                     in \n                    103m 27s\n                </p>\n                \n\n                \n                <p class=\"meta\" style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);\">\n                    <strong>Started:</strong> Jan 17, 2026 at 4:56 PM &middot;\n                    <strong>Ended:</strong> Jan 17, 2026 at 6:40 PM\n                </p>\n                \n            </header>\n\n            <div class=\"stats\">\n                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n                    <div class=\"value\">51,257</div>\n                    <div class=\"label\">Words</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n                    <div class=\"value\">5h 34m</div>\n                    <div class=\"label\">Est. Duration</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n                    <div class=\"value\">7</div>\n                    <div class=\"label\">Chapters</div>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n                    <div class=\"value\">12</div>\n                    <div class=\"label\">Main Characters</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n                    <div class=\"value\">628</div>\n                    <div class=\"label\">Pronunciation Notes</div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            \n            <section>\n                <h2>📚 Book Structure</h2>\n                \n                <p style=\"margin-top: 1rem; line-height: 1.8;\">This book contains 7 chapters. Chapters have descriptive titles.</p>\n                \n                \n            </section>\n\n            \n            <section>\n                <h2>📖 Plot Summary</h2>\n                <div style=\"margin-top: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; white-space: pre-wrap;\">The elevator boy, Nick Carraway, arrives in West Egg, renting a modest house near the extravagant mansions of Daisy and Tom Buchanan and the enigmatic Jay Gatsby. His introduction to the world of East Egg begins with a dinner at Daisy and Tom’s Georgian Colonial, where he witnesses Tom’s arrogance and racism, Daisy’s fragile charm, and Jordan Baker’s quiet deceit. The evening culminates in a violent outburst when Tom breaks Myrtle Wilson’s nose after she mentions Daisy, leading Nick to the Valley of Ashes and into the chaotic world of Myrtle’s affair with Tom. That night, Nick stumbles upon Gatsby’s mansion during a wild party, where he meets the elusive host—charming, mysterious, and radiating a rare, almost painful smile. Gatsby’s obsession with Daisy, whom he once loved in Louisville, becomes clear through Jordan’s recollections and Gatsby’s elaborate plan to reunite with her, including buying a mansion across the bay and orchestrating a tea at Nick’s house.\n\nThe rising action centers on Gatsby’s desperate attempt to reclaim his past with Daisy. After a rain-soaked reunion that moves Daisy to tears, Gatsby’s dream seems within reach—until Tom Buchanan arrives at Gatsby’s party, exposing his criminal past and bootlegging ties through Meyer Wolfsheim. The tension escalates during a drive to New York, where Tom forces Gatsby to confront Daisy, demanding she admit she never loved him. When Daisy hesitates and admits she once loved both men, Gatsby’s dream begins to shatter. The climax occurs in the Plaza Hotel when Myrtle is struck and killed by a speeding yellow car—Daisy, driving, flees the scene. Tom, knowing the truth, manipulates the situation, telling George Wilson that Gatsby owned the car. Wilson, consumed by grief and delusion, tracks Gatsby down and murders him before taking his own life, leaving Nick to confront the devastating consequences of the East’s moral decay.\n\nIn the aftermath, Nick is left isolated, grappling with the betrayal and emptiness of the world he once admired. Gatsby’s funeral is a hollow spectacle—his former guests vanish, and only his father, Henry C. Gatz, and a few strangers attend. Nick, haunted by the futility of Gatsby’s dream, reflects on the American ideal corrupted by wealth and dishonesty. He confronts Tom, who admits to lying to Wilson, and realizes the depth of his own disillusionment. Returning to the Midwest, Nick revisits Gatsby’s abandoned mansion, erases a vulgar graffito, and watches the moon rise over the bay, meditating on the human condition: the relentless pursuit of an unattainable past, the illusion of reinvention, and the tragic beauty of striving toward a green light that was never meant to be reached.</div>\n                \n                <p style=\"margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--muted);\">\n                    <strong>Themes:</strong> identity, ambition, loss\n                </p>\n                \n            </section>\n            \n\n            \n            <section>\n                <h2>🤖 Analysis Models</h2>\n                <table style=\"width: 100%; margin-top: 1rem; border-collapse: collapse;\">\n                    <thead>\n                        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 2px solid var(--primary);\">\n                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Phase</th>\n                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Model</th>\n                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Provider</th>\n                        </tr>\n                    </thead>\n                    <tbody>\n                        \n                        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--primary);\">\n                            <td style=\"padding: 0.75rem;\">Chapter Detection</td>\n                            <td style=\"padding: 0.75rem; font-family: monospace;\">qwen3:30b-instruct</